{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-08-02-summer-fruits-around-the-world/audio/main-f3e08c4507fa.mp3","durationSec":325.536,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.94,"text":"On a hot day, cold and juicy fruit can feel very refreshing."},{"start":4.78,"end":9.34,"text":"However, summer fruits around the world do more than help people feel cool."},{"start":10.02,"end":13.26,"text":"They can also tell a story about weather, place, and daily life."},{"start":14.14,"end":17.22,"text":"A family may cut one large fruit and share it after dinner."},{"start":17.86,"end":21.36,"text":"A street seller may prepare a small fruit snack for one customer."},{"start":22.14,"end":25.94,"text":"In a tropical orchard, visitors can taste fruit near the trees where it grows."},{"start":26.82,"end":30.86,"text":"In a northern forest, people may carry baskets and look for wild berries."},{"start":31.82,"end":34.88,"text":"These are different activities, but fruit connects all of them."},{"start":35.68,"end":40.86,"text":"To understand a fruit culture, we can ask where the fruit grows, how people prepare it, and who eats it together."},{"start":42.1,"end":45.46,"text":"Watermelon and melon are important summer fruits in Spanish homes."},{"start":46.16,"end":53.36,"text":"Between June 2024 and May 2025, homes in Spain bought more than 660 million kilos of these two fruits."},{"start":54,"end":56.18,"text":"Their seasons are not exactly the same."},{"start":57.16,"end":62.36,"text":"Watermelon is most popular in the middle of summer, while people continue to buy melon into early autumn."},{"start":63.16,"end":67.76,"text":"This difference is useful when you shop: the best choice can change from one month to the next."},{"start":68.5,"end":71.62,"text":"Watermelon is often served cold and cut into large pieces."},{"start":72.22,"end":76.1,"text":"For example, a family can put a bowl of cold pieces on the table after lunch."},{"start":76.66,"end":81.58,"text":"At a picnic or the beach, one large watermelon is also easy for several people to share."},{"start":82.36,"end":85.48,"text":"Thailand offers a very different summer fruit experience."},{"start":85.98,"end":92.74,"text":"In Rayong, orchard visits are especially interesting in June and July, when rain has made the land green and many fruits are ready."},{"start":93.2,"end":97.44,"text":"Visitors can ride through an orchard, stop near the trees, and then enjoy a fruit buffet."},{"start":98.16,"end":103.96,"text":"They may see soft-haired rambutan, purple mangosteen, large jackfruit, and heavy durian."},{"start":104.76,"end":108.1,"text":"Mangosteen has white pieces inside and a sweet-and-sour taste."},{"start":109.1,"end":113.08,"text":"Durian has a powerful smell, but its inside is soft, rich, and sweet."},{"start":113.74,"end":117.44,"text":"The buffet may also include mango with sticky rice and coconut milk."},{"start":119,"end":122.38,"text":"This example shows that fruit tourism is not only about eating."},{"start":122.38,"end":128.28,"text":"Visitors also see where the food grows and compare new smells, shapes, and textures."},{"start":130.1,"end":132.86,"text":"India's hot season brings several special fruits."},{"start":132.86,"end":141.44,"text":"Litchi is a small, juicy fruit with a rough red skin, and it is harvested in summer in places such as East Champaran in Bihar."},{"start":142.4,"end":145.08,"text":"Mango also becomes the centre of public celebrations."},{"start":145.76,"end":154.5,"text":"At the Krishnagiri Mango Festival in Tamil Nadu, visitors can see different kinds of mango and foods such as pickles, juices, curries, and desserts."},{"start":155.88,"end":157.82,"text":"Jackfruit gives us another useful lesson."},{"start":158.6,"end":165.12,"text":"A ripe jackfruit has sweet yellow fruit inside, so people can eat it as a dessert or preserve it in syrup."},{"start":166.26,"end":171.74,"text":"A mature but unripe jackfruit can become chips, and tender jackfruit can be cooked as a vegetable."},{"start":172.58,"end":176.1,"text":"The same fruit can therefore move from a sweet snack to a savoury meal."},{"start":177.7,"end":181.4,"text":"In Mexico, mango season runs mainly from April to August."},{"start":182.44,"end":189.16,"text":"Mango can be eaten fresh, but it also appears in juices, ice cream, sweets, fruit cups, and frozen snacks."},{"start":190.72,"end":196.62,"text":"One very concrete street-food example is mango prepared with chile, lime, and salt."},{"start":197.42,"end":202.98,"text":"The mango is sweet, the lime is sour, the salt is salty, and the chile is spicy."},{"start":203.52,"end":206.96,"text":"This means one simple snack can bring four flavours together."},{"start":207.84,"end":215.7,"text":"Chamoy, a tangy sauce that is often sweet, sour, salty, and spicy, is also used in mango snacks called mangonadas."},{"start":216.7,"end":223.32,"text":"Imagine a seller cutting a ripe mango into a cup, squeezing lime over it, and adding a little chile and salt."},{"start":223.96,"end":227.5,"text":"The preparation changes the fruit without hiding its fresh taste."},{"start":228.34,"end":232.76,"text":"In Türkiye, the names of summer fruits are often connected to farming regions."},{"start":232.76,"end":240,"text":"Malatya is known for apricots, Aydın for figs, and Kırkağaç in Manisa Province for melons."},{"start":240.74,"end":244.12,"text":"These names help shoppers connect a fruit with the place where it grows."},{"start":244.96,"end":253.56,"text":"In June, fresh apricots, figs, and melons begin to fill markets, while watermelon is another major summer favourite."},{"start":253.56,"end":260.78,"text":"Fresh apricots are soft and slightly sharp, but drying them makes their taste stronger and lets people keep them longer."},{"start":261.8,"end":264.06,"text":"Figs can also be eaten fresh or dried."},{"start":264.9,"end":272.68,"text":"Here is a simple family example: a plate of sliced melon, fresh figs, and apricots can sit in the middle of the table after a meal."},{"start":273.3,"end":275.86,"text":"Everyone can take a piece and continue talking."},{"start":276.9,"end":281.5,"text":"Lithuania has a short warm season, so the arrival of berries can feel special."},{"start":282.14,"end":288.62,"text":"In Dzūkija, a forest region in the south of the country, looking for mushrooms and berries is a traditional activity."},{"start":289.26,"end":292.8,"text":"Wild blueberries are one of the foods that people can collect there."},{"start":293.38,"end":296.28,"text":"The experience is very different from buying fruit in a shop."},{"start":296.94,"end":303.68,"text":"A person carries a basket, walks slowly, looks carefully near the ground, and chooses only ripe berries."},{"start":304.84,"end":307.62,"text":"It also takes time and local knowledge."},{"start":308.24,"end":313.72,"text":"For example, a family might spend a quiet morning in the forest and bring a small basket home."},{"start":314.54,"end":320.48,"text":"They can eat the berries fresh, add them to pancakes or yogurt, or make jam for colder months."},{"start":321.3,"end":324.9,"text":"The fruit becomes both food and a memory of time outdoors."}],"words":[{"text":"On","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"a","start":0.16,"end":0.28},{"text":"hot","start":0.28,"end":0.44},{"text":"day","start":0.44,"end":0.86},{"text":"cold","start":1.34,"end":1.58},{"text":"and","start":1.58,"end":1.82},{"text":"juicy","start":1.82,"end":2.12},{"text":"fruit","start":2.12,"end":2.5},{"text":"can","start":2.5,"end":2.68},{"text":"feel","start":2.68,"end":2.94},{"text":"very","start":2.94,"end":3.38},{"text":"refreshing","start":3.38,"end":3.94},{"text":"However","start":4.78,"end":5.3},{"text":"summer","start":6.04,"end":6.18},{"text":"fruits","start":6.18,"end":6.56},{"text":"around","start":6.56,"end":6.88},{"text":"the","start":6.88,"end":7.02},{"text":"world","start":7.02,"end":7.3},{"text":"do","start":7.3,"end":7.66},{"text":"m